---
import CopyButton from '../../components/CopyButton.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const install = 'npm install @bryllim/workout-guide';
const api = `import {
  exercises,
  getExercise,
  searchExercises,
  getAssetUrl,
} from '@bryllim/workout-guide';

const pushUp = getExercise('push-up');
const results = searchExercises('chest bodyweight');
const imageUrl = getAssetUrl('push-up', 1);`;
const direct = `import frame1 from '@bryllim/workout-guide/assets/push-up/frame-1.svg';

export function ExerciseImage() {
  return <img src={frame1} alt="Push-up starting position" />;
}`;
const manifest = `import manifest from '@bryllim/workout-guide/manifest.json';

console.log(manifest.length); // 302`;
const expo = `// React Native bundlers need literal require() paths.
const pushUpFrames = [
  require('@bryllim/workout-guide/assets/push-up/frame-1.svg'),
  require('@bryllim/workout-guide/assets/push-up/frame-2.svg'),
  require('@bryllim/workout-guide/assets/push-up/frame-3.svg'),
];`;
const cdn = 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@bryllim/workout-guide@1.0.0/assets/push-up/frame-1.svg';
---

<BaseLayout title="Integration guide — Workout Guide" description="Install and integrate Workout Guide exercise assets in web, Expo, React Native, and other JavaScript projects.">
  <header class="page-intro page-shell"><div><p class="eyebrow">Framework-neutral</p><h1>Bring the frames into your project.</h1></div><p>Use the typed API, import assets directly, or load immutable versioned URLs from a CDN.</p></header>
  <div class="guide-layout page-shell section">
    <nav class="guide-nav" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#install">Install</a><a href="#api">JavaScript API</a><a href="#assets">Direct assets</a><a href="#native">Expo / React Native</a><a href="#cdn">CDN</a><a href="#license">Licensing</a></nav>
    <div class="guide-content">
      <section class="guide-section" id="install"><p class="eyebrow">01</p><h2>Install</h2><p>The package ships dual ESM and CommonJS builds, TypeScript declarations, a JSON manifest, and all 906 SVG assets.</p><div class="code-with-copy"><CopyButton text={install} /><div class="code-block" data-squircle data-radius="24"><pre tabindex="0"><code>{install}</code></pre></div></div></section>
      <section class="guide-section" id="api"><p class="eyebrow">02</p><h2>JavaScript API</h2><p>Look up exact exercises or search the normalized catalog with optional equipment, muscle, type, and stretch filters.</p><div class="code-with-copy"><CopyButton text={api} /><div class="code-block" data-squircle data-radius="24"><pre tabindex="0"><code>{api}</code></pre></div></div><h3>Raw manifest</h3><div class="code-with-copy"><CopyButton text={manifest} /><div class="code-block" data-squircle data-radius="24"><pre tabindex="0"><code>{manifest}</code></pre></div></div></section>
      <section class="guide-section" id="assets"><p class="eyebrow">03</p><h2>Direct static imports</h2><p>Every asset uses the stable path <code>assets/&lt;slug&gt;/frame-&lt;1|2|3&gt;.svg</code>.</p><div class="code-with-copy"><CopyButton text={direct} /><div class="code-block" data-squircle data-radius="24"><pre tabindex="0"><code>{direct}</code></pre></div></div></section>
      <section class="guide-section" id="native"><p class="eyebrow">04</p><h2>Expo and React Native</h2><p>Metro resolves static assets at build time, so keep each <code>require()</code> path literal. Do not assemble these paths dynamically.</p><div class="code-with-copy"><CopyButton text={expo} /><div class="code-block" data-squircle data-radius="24"><pre tabindex="0"><code>{expo}</code></pre></div></div></section>
      <section class="guide-section" id="cdn"><p class="eyebrow">05</p><h2>Versioned CDN URLs</h2><p>Pin a package version for stable production URLs. The <code>getAssetUrl()</code> helper generates the same pattern.</p><div class="code-with-copy"><CopyButton text={cdn} /><div class="code-block" data-squircle data-radius="24"><pre tabindex="0"><code>{cdn}</code></pre></div></div></section>
      <section class="guide-section" id="license"><p class="eyebrow">06</p><h2>Licensing and attribution</h2><p>Code and documentation are MIT licensed. Visual assets are CC BY-SA 4.0. The original pose artwork comes from Everkinetic and was expanded upon by Bryl Lim; direct source details are included in the manifest.</p><div class="guide-card" data-squircle data-radius="32"><p><strong>Suggested credit</strong></p><p>Original exercise artwork by <a href="https://github.com/everkinetic/data">Everkinetic</a>, expanded by <a href="https://bryllim.com">Bryl Lim</a>, licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>.</p></div></section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
